@model UBookIt.Web.Rendering.CancellationPageModel
@{
    Layout = null;
    var zone = Model.TimeZoneId;
}
@*
    WHAT THIS PAGE MAY SAY, and what it structurally cannot.

    It names the booking — reference, what was booked, when — because the secret that reached here
    is already sufficient to DESTROY the booking, so withholding a description of what is about to
    be destroyed protects nothing and costs the reader the one fact they need: which booking this
    is. Somebody holding three bookings and three messages cannot otherwise tell which link they
    followed.

    It cannot name the BOOKER. Not by restraint — the model has no member for a name, an address or
    a telephone number, so this holds however the view is written, including by a theme.

    The action is a POST. Mail scanners fetch every URL in a message unattended; a GET that
    cancelled would let robots cancel bookings before the person had read the message.
*@
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <title>Cancel your booking</title>
</head>
<body>
    <main class="cancel">
        <h1>Cancel this booking?</h1>

        <dl class="cancel-booking">
            <dt>Reference</dt>
            <dd>@Model.Reference</dd>

            <dt>When</dt>
            <dd>
                <time datetime="@Model.LocalStart.ToString("o")">
                    @Model.LocalStart.ToString("dddd d MMMM yyyy, HH:mm")
                </time>
                &ndash;
                <time datetime="@Model.LocalEnd.ToString("o")">
                    @Model.LocalEnd.ToString("HH:mm")
                </time>
                <span class="cancel-zone">(@zone)</span>
            </dd>

            @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model.ServiceName))
            {
                <dt>Service</dt>
                <dd>@Model.ServiceName</dd>
            }

            @if (Model.ResourceNames.Count > 0)
            {
                <dt>@(Model.ResourceNames.Count == 1 ? "Resource" : "Resources")</dt>
                <dd>
                    <ul class="cancel-resources">
                        @foreach (var name in Model.ResourceNames)
                        {
                            <li>@name</li>
                        }
                    </ul>
                </dd>
            }
        </dl>

        <p>This cannot be undone. If you still want the booking, you can simply close this page.</p>

        @*
            NO ACTION ATTRIBUTE, deliberately. An empty action posts to the URL this page was
            fetched from, which is the same route with the same secret — so the secret never
            appears in the MARKUP, only in the address. A hidden field carrying it would put a
            credential into the document body, where a copied page source or a "save page as"
            carries it too.
        *@
        <form method="post">
            @Html.AntiForgeryToken()
            <button type="submit">Cancel this booking</button>
        </form>
    </main>
</body>
</html>
